{"name":"Blue Mountain","hex":"#759dbe","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"blue","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a blue hue.","Depressed, melancholic, sad."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour of the clear sky or the deep sea; the colour midway between green and violet in the visible spectrum and one of the primary additive colours.","Anything coloured blue, especially to distinguish it from similar objects differing only in colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue"},{"term":"mountain","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An elevation of land of considerable dimensions rising more or less abruptly, forming a conspicuous figure in the landscape, usually having a small extent of surface at its summit. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","Something very large in size or quantity; a huge amount; a great heap."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mountain"}],"entries":[{"title":"Blue Mountain (British Columbia)","blocks":[{"text":"Blue Mountain is a mountain in British Columbia."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue_Mountain_(British_Columbia)","wikidata":"Q4929490"},{"title":"Blue Mountain, Kings County, Nova Scotia","blocks":[{"text":"Blue Mountain is a community in the Canadian province of Nova Scotia, located in Kings County."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue_Mountain%2C_Kings_County%2C_Nova_Scotia","wikidata":"Q4929486"},{"title":"Blue Mountain (ski resort)","blocks":[{"text":"Blue Mountain Resorts is a ski resort located in The Blue Mountains, Ontario, Canada. The resort spans the Niagara Escarpment near the southern shore of Georgian Bay, and encompasses 147 hectares of skiable terrain with a vertical drop of 220 metres (720 ft). As of 2024, the resort maintains 43 named runs, which includes its four terrain parks."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/20/Blue_Mountain_Resort_-_Summer_view.jpg/330px-Blue_Mountain_Resort_-_Summer_view.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue_Mountain_(ski_resort)","wikidata":"Q4929499"},{"title":"Mountain","blocks":[{"text":"A mountain is an elevated portion of the surface of a planet, generally with steep sides that show significant exposed bedrock. Although there are no universally accepted definitions, a mountain is usually considered higher than a hill. By definition, mountains are often thought of as being a landform which is higher than 2,000 feet (610 m). It may either have a limited summit area or be a smaller plateau with high elevation and steep sides. A few mountains are isolated summits, but most occur in mountain ranges."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e7/Everest_North_Face_toward_Base_Camp_Tibet_Luca_Galuzzi_2006.jpg/330px-Everest_North_Face_toward_Base_Camp_Tibet_Luca_Galuzzi_2006.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mountain","wikidata":"Q8502"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/47/2017-11-16-BMP_Bowl-5638.jpg/500px-2017-11-16-BMP_Bowl-5638.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/47/2017-11-16-BMP_Bowl-5638.jpg/1280px-2017-11-16-BMP_Bowl-5638.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/47/2017-11-16-BMP_Bowl-5638.jpg/500px-2017-11-16-BMP_Bowl-5638.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"BMP marking on a ceramic bowl to denote its makers, Blue Mountain Pottery. The pottery business was operated by Blue Mountain Resorts from 1953 to 1967 to support the resort's finances during the skiing off-season.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A2017-11-16-BMP_Bowl-5638.jpg"},{"srcs